cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference Hexnest, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Hexnest"
abstract: >-
  Hexnest is a free and open-source system utility for Windows 10, Windows 11 and
  macOS 12 or newer. On both platforms it provides a live system monitor with
  per-core processor load and per-application resource usage, a network monitor with
  per-application traffic, a start-up manager and a disk cleaner that measures rather
  than estimates. On Windows it is additionally a driver scanner, installer and
  updater: it enumerates every present PnP device through SetupAPI and CfgMgr32,
  reports which devices have no driver, installs missing and outdated drivers from
  the Windows Update catalog or from local INF folders, resumes its install queue
  after the restarts a driver install requires, and backs drivers up so they can be
  restored offline from a USB stick after a format. The Windows build ships as a
  single self-contained executable and the macOS build as an application bundle;
  neither needs a runtime installed first.
